From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:21:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246: The top
 amplifier is an AW88263
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The top speaker amplifier on this unit answers on I2C with chip ID
0x2032, the AW88263's, not the AW88261's 0x2113, and the AW88261 driver
rejects it. The vendor firmware carries profiles for both parts, so
either may be fitted; describe the one this unit has.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts   | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
index a37ed9ca7..d1d027fb3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
@@ -439,8 +439,13 @@ &gpu_zap_shader {
 &i2c0 {
 	status = "okay";
 
+	/*
+	 * The vendor firmware carries profiles for both the AW88261 and the
+	 * AW88263, so either may be fitted; the unit this was brought up on
+	 * answers with the AW88263's chip ID.
+	 */
 	amp_top: audio-codec@34 {
-		compatible = "awinic,aw88261";
+		compatible = "awinic,aw88263";
 		reg = <0x34>;
 
 		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 26 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
